displays.description:
The display card on the dashboard and any wall panels. The display colors are used for the glucose value and for everything else that shows a zone by color; the graph range colors only for the range bands of the graphs. Color is never the only cue: the zone word under the glucose value names the zone in every setting. On a chosen background the text is black or white, whichever contrasts more, and the graphs keep their black area. The CGM Report keeps the colors of the published report examples.

**Contrast of the saved colors:** {contrast_note} The note changes no color; the chosen colors are always used. The minimums are those of the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.2: 4.5:1 for text and 3:1 for large text such as the glucose value (World Wide Web Consortium, 2024). The default graph range colors are those of the CGM Report's glucose profile. The setting *Outline text* draws an edge around the graph labels and the text in a zone color.

**Wall-panel address:** {panel_address}

